        "lines": [
          {
            "id": "taylor",
            "text": "$f(x_0 + h, y_0 + k) - f(x_0, y_0) \\approx \\tfrac{1}{2}(Ah^2 + 2Bhk + Ck^2)$, second-order Taylor; the linear part is 0 since $\\nabla f = \\mathbf{0}$"
          },
          {
            "id": "square",
            "text": "$Ah^2 + 2Bhk + Ck^2 = A\\left(h + \\tfrac{B}{A}k\\right)^2 + \\left(C - \\tfrac{B^2}{A}\\right)k^2$, complete the square in $h$ (with $A \\neq 0$)"
          },
          {
            "id": "dee",
            "text": "$= A\\left(h + \\tfrac{B}{A}k\\right)^2 + \\tfrac{D}{A}k^2$, since $C - \\tfrac{B^2}{A} = \\tfrac{AC - B^2}{A}$"
          },
          {
            "id": "verdict",
            "text": "So if $D > 0$ both terms have the sign of $A$; if $D < 0$ they have opposite signs"
